WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.821 --> 00:00:05.141
- [Narrator] On the outside, this chapel

00:00:05.141 --> 00:00:07.469
looks like a normal cathedral.

00:00:07.469 --> 00:00:09.920
But on the inside, it's a gilded triumph

00:00:09.920 --> 00:00:12.251
to the Catholic faith.

00:00:12.251 --> 00:00:15.168
Welcome to the Capilla del Rosario.

00:00:21.101 --> 00:00:23.653
The Capilla del Rosario, or Rosary Chapel,

00:00:23.653 --> 00:00:25.552
is found inside the
Church of Santo Domingo

00:00:25.552 --> 00:00:27.352
in Puebla, Mexico.

00:00:27.352 --> 00:00:29.021
It was built in the 17th century

00:00:29.021 --> 00:00:31.160
between 1650 and 1690

00:00:31.160 --> 00:00:32.520
and was the first chapel in Mexico

00:00:32.520 --> 00:00:34.519
dedicated to Our Lady of the Rosary,

00:00:34.519 --> 00:00:36.811
or the Virgin Mary.

00:00:36.811 --> 00:00:39.091
The chapel, with it's gold
leaf and ornate details,

00:00:39.091 --> 00:00:41.752
has been considered the
eighth wonder of the world.

00:00:41.752 --> 00:00:43.752
In 1979, Pope John Paul II

00:00:43.752 --> 00:00:47.520
called the Rosary Chapel
a reliquary of America.

00:00:47.520 --> 00:00:49.880
A shining example of Mexican
baroque architecture,

00:00:49.880 --> 00:00:52.552
the chapel has ornate
sculptures, oil paintings,

00:00:52.552 --> 00:00:57.080
statues, and moldings covered
in 23 karat gold leaf.

00:00:57.080 --> 00:00:59.291
The centerpiece of the
sanctuary is an altar

00:00:59.291 --> 00:01:01.651
dedicated to the Virgin Mary.

00:01:01.651 --> 00:01:03.832
Even with enough gold to
fill a secure bank safe,

00:01:03.832 --> 00:01:06.360
the church regularly holds
mass and other services

00:01:06.360 --> 00:01:08.358
for worshipers.

00:01:08.358 --> 00:01:10.461
Anyone, religious or not, can appreciate

00:01:10.461 --> 00:01:14.044
the golden glow of the
Capilla del Rosario.

